{ "run_id": "...", "reason": "credential_window|provider_exhausted|upstream_unavailable|crash_interrupted|reauth_required", "retry_after_ms": 52260000 /*omitted when unknown*/, "resets_at": "2026-10-18T06:00:00Z" /*omitted when unknown*/ }

// Env
EXECUTION_LOOP_PARKING_ENABLED (execution-core, default false). SESSION_CORE_PARK_TTL_SECONDS (session-core, default 86400). Existing: SESSION_CORE_LOOP_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED gates the store AND (new) all recovery-worker fold logic. EXECUTION_LOOP_CHECKPOINT_ENABLED (S6) is needed only for CrashInterrupted (no round folds, nothing to crash-park).

// Park row semantics (run_loop_checkpoints; no migration needed, the 0047 columns suffice)
state='parked', kind='park', pause_ref=park_ref, park_reason, park_until (earliest useful resume time, not the TTL), seq CAS. TTL = updated_at + park_ttl. The row columns, not the fold body, are authoritative for pause_ref and park_reason (a crash park re-seals the body to match anyway).
